---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import '../styles/prose.css'
---

<Base
  title="About · Replant Blog"
  description="Why we write. Placeholder until Founder drafts the final copy."
>
  <article>
    <header class="header">
      <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
      <h1>Why we <em>write</em>.</h1>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        <strong>This page is a placeholder.</strong> Founder will draft the
        final copy before the blog ships to a public DNS. The shape below is
        what the page will hold:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>One paragraph on what Replant is — a secure communication platform for Christian leaders globally, with particular care for the persecuted church.</li>
        <li>One paragraph on what this blog is for — a quieter surface, sporadic by design, for letters and field reports.</li>
        <li>One paragraph on how readers can contact us — submission, prayer requests, partnership inquiries.</li>
        <li>A closing scripture or sentence.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        No author byline goes on this page. The blog speaks as <em>Replant</em>,
        not in any one person's voice.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  article { padding: 5rem 1.5rem 6rem; }
  .header {
    max-width: 68ch;
    margin: 0 auto 3rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.25em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--sky);
    margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
  }
  h1 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.2rem);
    line-height: 1.15;
    color: var(--ink);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  h1 em {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--sky);
  }
</style>
